    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0400" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chinese Foreign Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-19">May 19, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Dr. Soong</hi>: Apropos of your note of May
                        18th,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d108-f1"/> the only amendment I have to suggest
                    relates to paragraph 5 of your proposed wire to the Generalissimo. I think the
                    following wording would more appropriately indicate the President’s purposes
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“5. The President told me that it is the position of the United States
                            that 
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Anakim</hi>
                             will be undertaken this winter in conjunction with the British.
                            Definite plans for this project are now being considered from the
                            viewpoint of the allotment of tonnage and special equipment, preliminary
                            to detailed plans for each phase of the operation, which will be
                            communicated to me for your consideration as they are prepared.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Very cordially yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry L. Hopkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
